# ARK product brain (non-negotiable)

## Core identity

- **ARK owns its own brain.** Local inference, model storage, Local AI UI, and the localhost brain API are ARK Engine — not a wrapper around any third-party local app.
- ARK must **run without** Ollama (or similar) installed. Never make a third-party local runtime required.
- Do **not** treat Ollama as ARK’s brain, default engine, or identity.

## Pluggable model sources (including Ollama)

- **Ollama is just another plug-in source** — same idea as Hugging Face, GitHub Models, OpenRouter free routes, etc.
- Users enable it in Models, then use those models like any other model. No special “Ollama mode” identity.
- Same pattern for any free/open source the user wants to attach.

## Free model discovery mission

ARK should **find and lock in free coding / creation capacity** so users are not stuck hunting APIs or waiting out rate limits:

- Prefer free local ARK Engine models first.
- Continuously surface free cloud options: GitHub Models, Hugging Face Inference, OpenRouter free routes, Google AI Studio free tier, Groq free tier, Pollinations-style free media, etc.
- When a free key or no-key endpoint works, wire it into Models / Chat / Image / Video so the user just picks and creates.
- Hardware-fit recommendations stay; search can still find anything (including heavy or external sources).

## Models page behavior

- Keep **For your PC** (best / balanced / performance).
- Default lists = hardware-fit only.
- Search = intentional discovery (out-of-spec, Ollama, HF, etc. can appear).

## Generated media

- Image / video outputs must be **real media** when a free/local/cloud path is available — not text-on-gradient placeholders presented as finished art.
- Generations are **saved into Recent → Creations** (and ARK Engine media storage) so users can reopen them.
- Be honest in UI if only a preview/fallback was produced.

## Lindsay / brain API

- External clients (Lindsay, other assistants, agents) talk to **ARK’s** brain API / engine on `127.0.0.1:8787`.
- Ollama-shaped `/api/*` and OpenAI-shaped `/v1/chat/completions` exist so apps that used Ollama can point at ARK instead.
- Optional bridges (Ollama, HF, …) are add-ons *into* ARK — never the core dependency.
- Cookbook: `docs/ark-brain-api.md` · sample: `examples/external-brain-client/`.
